        <section id="user-experience-and-user-interface" >
          
            <h2>User experience and User interface</h2>
              <p>UI and UX design are different, but are also related design disciplines. A user interface is where a ‘human would interact with a machine’.  User experience is the experience a person has when they interact with a product. UX design is more analytical and would consider cognitive behaviour and human psychology.</p>
<p><img src="~/images/svg/cp3/cp3_u2_s5_p1_image2.svg" alt=""></p>

          
        </section>
        
    
     
    
  
     
    
  
  
        <section id="differences-between-ui-and-ux" >
          
            <h2>Differences between UI and UX</h2>
              <p>See below to see the differences between UI and UX:</p>

              
              
  <div class="toggle-group">
  
<toggle-section open="false">
    <h3>User experience (UX)</h3>
    <p>UX is the experience a user would have when interacting with a product, service, application, or system. It would consider the user’s attitude and emotions when designing products that are easy to use and understand.</p>
<p>UX focuses on:</p>
<ul>
<li>Customer Research</li>
<li>User Testing</li>
<li>Development</li>
<li>Content</li>
<li>Usability</li>
<li>Ease of use</li>
<li>Pleasure</li>
<li>Prototyping to test for quality results</li>
</ul>

</toggle-section>
  
<toggle-section open="false">
    <h3>User interface (UI)</h3>
    <p>UI deals with the interaction of the individual to a service, system, or application. It will allow a user to operate a device such as a computer, tablet or phone to complete a task or achieve a specific goal (e.g. use an online website to purchase an item).</p>
<p>The three main forms of user interfaces are:</p>
<ul>
<li>graphic user interface (GUI),</li>
<li>command line interface,</li>
<li>or a voice-enabled user interface.</li>
</ul>
<p>They are composed of input hardware (e.g. a mouse or keyboard), and output hardware such as a monitor or audio speakers.</p>
<p>UI focuses on:</p>
<ul>
<li>User-friendly experience</li>
<li>Human-computer interaction</li>
<li>Graphical controls</li>
<li>Layout</li>
<li>Design</li>
<li>Branding</li>
<li>Visual elements</li>
</ul>

</toggle-section>
</div>

            
          
        </section>
        
    
     
    
  
  
